GraphCast
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The graphcast/ directory is a modified copy of DeepMind's GraphCast code
(https://github.com/google-deepmind/graphcast, commit
8debd7289bb2c498485f79dbd98d8b4933bfc6a7),
Copyright 2023 DeepMind Technologies Limited, licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. Files changed from that commit (each also carries a notice at the top):

  autoregressive.py         adds per_timestep_loss_and_diagnostics (the loss at each
                            forecast step); uses xarray .sizes instead of .dims for
                            dimension lengths
  data_utils.py             adds a 'justify' option to extract_inputs_targets_forcings
                            ('left', the default, takes the inputs from the start of the
                            dataset; 'right' is the upstream behavior); prints the
                            target lead times
  deep_typed_graph_net.py   adds optional per-layer rematerialization (hk.remat) of the
                            processor (checkpoint_processor; same math, less memory;
                            off by default)
  graphcast.py              at import, reads the loss selection (variables, levels,
                            lat/lon region) from the run config named by the j_path
                            environment variable; the loss is losses.custom_weighted_mse;
                            precipitation loss weight 0.0 (upstream 0.1); processor
                            rematerialization on; logging setup
  losses.py                 adds custom_weighted_mse (the weighted MSE of
                            weighted_mse_per_level with optional variable/level/region
                            selection), point_mse and retain_per_variable_losses;
                            sum_per_variable_losses returns the weighted per-variable
                            losses as diagnostics (the total is unchanged); the latitude
                            check for grids without poles accepts regional subsets;
                            logging setup
  rollout.py                uses xarray .sizes instead of .dims for dimension lengths
  solar_radiation.py        uses typing.Union instead of X | Y annotations (Python 3.9);
                            data_array_like in get_toa_incident_solar_radiation_for_xarray
                            defaults to None

graphcast/__init__.py is new (package marker). All other files in graphcast/ are
unchanged from that commit. The upstream test files (*_test.py) are not included.

